{
  "comment": "Each make target of CHECK_TARGETS declares its scope and the setup steps it needs: needs [\"databases\"] is a target that reads the servers of make test-servers and the bench and decimal databases of the run, which the runner records as not-run, with the failed step and its first failure lines, when the setup step servers or databases/create fails; needs [] runs whatever the setup steps did. An owner target is a per-file check (format, checklist, documents, the unit tests of a checker): make owner-check runs it when a changed path matches its inputs. A suite target is part of the full suite only: make check runs it once, and make owner-check never selects it; a changed feature's own verification and coverage run in its place. make owner-check and make repo-check fail on a target without a scope, an owner target without inputs, a suite target with inputs, and an input pattern that matches no tracked file. A pattern matches a repository path: * within one path segment, ** across segments.",
